{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1483252-changelings-and-the-ecstatic-wind","id":1483252,"title":"Changelings and the Ecstatic Wind","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-06T14:24:01-07:00","id":1483252,"title":"Changelings and the Ecstatic Wind","content":"I'll preface this by saying it's been a very, very long time since I last read <i>Astral Realms</i> and I do not possess a copy of the book, so some (many) of the finer nuances of the Anima Mundi and what it's meant to represent will probably escape me here.<br /> <br /> According to the <i>Beast Player's Guide</i>, changelings who die in dream form while in the Mother's Land &quot;lose any current oaths&quot; when they wake. No further comment is added, which leaves the intention a little ambiguous, and with worrying implications considering what oaths mean from a Lost perspective. Muddying the waters is that the Player's Guide was published before the final version of Lost, and looking at the credits for the books, it looks like neither Rose Bailey nor Meghan Fitzgerald was involved in the writing or development of the Player's Guide, while author overlap between the two books is minimal.<br /> <br /> Essentially: When changelings die from the Ecstatic Winds, should they lose all active oaths as they are ultimately defined in 2nd Edition? And if so, do they count as having broken them? That's almost guaranteed social death for a changeling in many situations (not to mention the Clarity damage), to say nothing of the consequences of sudden Mantle loss.<br /> <br /> If the author is using &quot;oaths&quot; here in a glossed or 1st Edition sense, what would be an appropriate effect for 2E changelings to suffer instead? For the sake of comparison, Beasts lose a Chamber, mages suffer a Paradox Condition, Prometheans lose a dot of Pilgrimage, demons lose a dot of Cover, and vampires wake in frenzy. The common thread for most of these downsides seems to be a disconnect from humanity to a degree, as the dreamer's monstrosity is brought to the foreground (with Beasts being the notable exception to this thematic, but which can be explained as the Mother's Land ripping away at the place of their inner selves). In that case, perhaps losing all bargains, or the last bargain the Lost made, would be more in line with what overexposure to the Sidereal Wastes is supposed to represent. Other possibilities that come to mind include the loss of an Icon, an imposed Clarity Condition, or automatically spreading Bedlam for a Wyrd-determined period of time.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps, in the end, &quot;oaths&quot; really does mean oaths in the 2E sense of the term, these most heartfelt of pledges not necessarily broken but simply erased as though they were never sworn in the first place. Motleymates and Court leaders might be understanding enough to allow the hapless changeling to renew their vows (and it's really just a little bit of Glamour, a few more hopes, dreams, and weird mushrooms harvested here and there). Between then and now, however, the Lost will be in a very precarious position, making exploring the realms of dreams outside natural fae understanding a very risky proposition indeed. Perhaps there's a good reason why the n\u00e4ck will never be a child of God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T15:11:57-07:00","id":1483256,"title":"","content":"The Ecstatic Wind rends the boundaries between your individual self and the wider world, which itself does not bother with formalized relationships except as a put-on. Changelings lose their oaths when the Mother's Land gets too far into their souls because those are the things that they use to contextualize themselves as fae creatures, just as Beasts lose bits of their hold on the world outside the Cave and mages crack the borders of their human identity.<br /> <br /> A changeling without oaths is cut off from the framework that affords him a safety net in his day-to-day life, but while oaths are important in changeling society the text has never pretended that individual oaths are categorically life-changing \u2014 you set the terms of an oath when you swear it, and the permanence of an oath's place in your identity doesn't stop courtiers from renewing their vows at every turning of the seasons/changing of the guard/year and a day/etc.<br /> <br /> Given the thematic bent of how the Ecstatic Wind works, it does feel entirely suited for powerful changelings with a lot of active oaths to suffer a number of Clarity attacks likely to boot them into a Comatose state or set a wild entitlement to Bedlam \u2014 recall that mummies killed by the Wind immediately enter a state where they're wandering through their own memories to come back to life \u2014 but I'd definitely limit that to <i>active </i>oaths \u2014 just because you've clarified your status as a member of the Winter Court four and twenty times since your escape shouldn't mean you've got a statistically high likelihood of hitting severe Clarity damage from that alone, for all that the well-connected wayward one has more to lose from venturing into a place as close to Arcadia as a non-fae dimension is likely to get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T21:43:46-07:00","id":1483278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1483252-changelings-and-the-ecstatic-wind?p=1483256#post1483256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ecstatic Wind rends the boundaries between your individual self and the wider world, which itself does not bother with formalized relationships except as a put-on. Changelings lose their oaths when the Mother's Land gets too far into their souls because those are the things that they use to contextualize themselves as fae creatures, just as Beasts lose bits of their hold on the world outside the Cave and mages crack the borders of their human identity.<br /> <br /> A changeling without oaths is cut off from the framework that affords him a safety net in his day-to-day life, but while oaths are important in changeling society the text has never pretended that individual oaths are categorically life-changing \u2014 you set the terms of an oath when you swear it, and the permanence of an oath's place in your identity doesn't stop courtiers from renewing their vows at every turning of the seasons/changing of the guard/year and a day/etc.<br /> <br /> Given the thematic bent of how the Ecstatic Wind works, it does feel entirely suited for powerful changelings with a lot of active oaths to suffer a number of Clarity attacks likely to boot them into a Comatose state or set a wild entitlement to Bedlam \u2014 recall that mummies killed by the Wind immediately enter a state where they're wandering through their own memories to come back to life \u2014 but I'd definitely limit that to <i>active </i>oaths \u2014 just because you've clarified your status as a member of the Winter Court four and twenty times since your escape shouldn't mean you've got a statistically high likelihood of hitting severe Clarity damage from that alone, for all that the well-connected wayward one has more to lose from venturing into a place as close to Arcadia as a non-fae dimension is likely to get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, that's very sensible. So do you think these lost oaths are meant to be treated as broken, or simply obviated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T22:25:42-07:00","id":1483282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1483252-changelings-and-the-ecstatic-wind?p=1483278#post1483278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, that's very sensible. So do you think these lost oaths are meant to be treated as broken, or simply obviated?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former. Recouping your losses from a bad death in the Dreamtime should be comparable to making up for lost time claiming a wild entitlement or backing out of creating a new Court at the last minute.<br /> <br /> Also, the thing you lose from oaths is generally their benefits rather than their place in your history, and the fact that there are no mechanics or other places describing oaths as things you lose-as-in-no-longer-have indicates to me that the BPG wasn't throwing in a new ludonarrative device with no explanation in the middle of an otherwise clear list of consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-07-2022, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}